  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5901.13 Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5901.13 “Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR)” means a procedure used by a person trained in this technique to provide oxygen to the brain and heart through ventilations and by rhythmically increasing intrathoracic pressure.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at Chapter heading for Saf-C 5900) #12790, eff 5-24-19",
